-Hodgkin lymphoma and leukemia. The company conducts drug discovery, runs global clinical trials, and manufactures drugs independently. As of 2025, Brukinsa made up 74% of total revenue, while it has two other approved commercialized drugs in its portfolio, Beqalzi and Tevimbra. While Brukinsa has global leadership, the other two drugs generate revenue mostly from China. Based on Brukinsa, BeOne competes mainly with AbbVie and AstraZeneca. The company also has more than 50 drugs in clinical trials in its active pipeline, focused on other cancers.","desc_src":"Massive (formerly Polygon.io) ticker details","sic":"2834","sic_desc":"Pharmaceutical Preparations","sector":"Healthcare","industry":"Biotechnology","mcap":40584837701.97,"mcap_src":"Massive ticker details (2026-10-03)","shares":109786917,"shares_src":"Massive ticker details (share-class shares outstanding)","hq":"BASEL","website":"https://www.beonemedicines.com","employees":12000,"list_date":"2016-02-03","exchange":"XNAS","fy_end":"1231","cik":1651308,"massive_asof":"2026-10-03","sec_asof":"2026-10-03"},"fin":{"available":true,"src":"SEC EDGAR XBRL companyfacts","asof":"2026-10-03","q":[{"end":"2023-09-30","rev":781308000.0,"rev_yoy":101.6,"eps":0.16,"eps_yoy":"turned +","ni":215413000.0,"ni_yoy":"turned +","nm":27.6,"derived":null,"fp":null},{"end":"2023-12-31","rev":634409000.0,"rev_yoy":66.9,"eps":-0.27,"eps_yoy":18.2,"ni":-367553000.0,"ni_yoy":17.5,"nm":-57.9,"derived":["eps","rev","ni"],"fp":null},{"end":"2024-03-31","rev":751652000.0,"rev_yoy":67.9,"eps":-0.19,"eps_yoy":26.9,"ni":-251150000.0,"ni_yoy":27.9,"nm":-33.4,"derived":null,"fp":null},{"end":"2024-06-30","rev":929166000.0,"rev_yoy":56.1,"eps":-0.09,"eps_yoy":67.9,"ni":-120405000.0,"ni_yoy":68.4,"nm":-13.0,"derived":null,"fp":null},{"end":"2024-09-30","rev":1001599000.0,"rev_yoy":28.2,"eps":-0.09,"eps_yoy":-156.2,"ni":-121350000.0,"ni_yoy":-156.3,"nm":-12.1,"derived":null,"fp":null},{"end":"2024-12-31","rev":1127824000.0,"rev_yoy":77.8,"eps":-0.11